{
    "background_story": "Casen was a young Roman soldier who fought in the scorching deserts of North Africa. After a long day of battle, he would often retreat to the sudatorium, a steam-filled room in the Roman baths, to cleanse his body and clear his mind. The intense heat and humidity of the sudatorium helped to purify his skin and soothe his muscles, making him feel reborn. Casen became a regular at the baths, often meeting with fellow soldiers to share stories and strategies. The sudatorium became a sanctuary for him, a place where he could escape the brutality of war and find solace in the camaraderie of his comrades. As he rose through the ranks, Casen never forgot the rejuvenating power of the sudatorium, making sure to include similar facilities in the design of every Roman fort he commanded.",
